" Your Vim key config. Open it from the browser with :config; a running
" browser applies changes within a second of saving. Press ? on any page to
" see every key and command.
"
" This file is read after the built-in defaults (chrome/js/vim/defaults.vimrc),
" so anything here adds to or overrides them. The installer creates it once
" and never overwrites it.
"
" Syntax (like Tridactyl's rc file):
"   bind <keys> <command> [args...]
"   unbind <keys>
"   unbindall                  (start from nothing)
"   set <name> <value>
"   " and # start comments
"
" Keys: characters as typed (G is shift+g), <C-x> ctrl, <A-x> alt,
" <S-Insert> shift+insert, and <Esc> <Space> <CR> <Tab> <BS> <Up> <Down>
" <Left> <Right> <PageUp> <PageDown> <Home> <End> <F1>..<F12> <lt>.
" Sequences are written together: gg, gt, <C-w>c.
"
" Settings: hintchars, scrollstep (pixels), smoothscroll (true/false),
" timeout (ms to wait for the rest of a sequence), editor (program :config
" opens this file with, e.g. "set editor code"; Notepad if unset).
"
" Examples:
"   bind x tabclose
"   bind gh open https://github.com
"   unbind d
"   set scrollstep 120
"   set editor code
